  "answer_text": "If you want to watch MSNBC live online, the most important update is that **MSNBC rebranded to MS NOW** (short for *My Source for News, Opinion, and the World*). This change occurred after the network was spun off into a new company called Versant. \n\nWhen looking for official apps or streaming options, you should look for the name **MS NOW**. Because it is a premium cable news network, there is no permanent, completely free 24/7 legal video stream of MS NOW/MSNBC. However, there are several legal workarounds, free trials, and free audio options available:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Free Audio Streaming (Fully Free 24/7)\nIf you just want to listen to the live coverage of your favorite shows (like *Morning Joe*, *The Beat with Ari Melber*, or *The Rachel Maddow Show*), you can stream the **audio broadcast entirely for free**:\n* **TuneIn Radio:** The TuneIn app and website host the live, 24/7 audio stream of MS NOW for free. \n* **The MS NOW App:** You can download the official **MS NOW app** on iOS or Android and listen to live streaming audio of the broadcast without having to sign in.\n\n### 2. Live TV Streaming Free Trials\nTo watch the actual live TV broadcast, you can sign up for a live TV streaming service that carries the channel and use their free trial. Just remember to cancel before the trial period ends to avoid being charged:\n* **FuboTV:** Usually offers a **7-day free trial**.\n* **DirecTV Stream:** Often offers a **5-day free trial**.\n* **YouTube TV:** Typically offers a **7-day to 14-day free trial**.\n\n### 3. Stream Free with TV Provider Credentials\nIf you (or a family member) already pay for a traditional cable, satellite, or live TV subscription (like Sling Blue, Hulu + Live TV, Spectrum, or Comcast), you can watch for free.\n* Download the **MS NOW App** or visit the **NBC.com** (or MS NOW website) live stream section.\n* Select **Link TV Provider** and log in with your provider\u2019s username and password to unlock the continuous live stream.\n\n### 4. Watch Free Clips & Highlights on YouTube\nIf you don't need the continuous live channel but want to catch up on the day's political commentary, the official **MS NOW YouTube channel** uploaded clips of almost every major segment shortly after they air on television. This is completely free and requires no sign-ups or subscriptions.\n\n### 5. Free Live News Alternative: NBC News NOW\nIf you are simply looking for free live news without paying for a cable package, you can watch **NBC News NOW**. \n* *Note: This is a separate, free 24/7 streaming news network from NBC News (not the opinion-focused MS NOW)*. \n* You can stream NBC News NOW for 100% free on **YouTube, Pluto TV, Tubi, Plex, Samsung TV Plus**, and the free tier of **Peacock**.",
